```

This test method will verify the behavior of Add method. It tests if ArrayList.Add (object) adds an item to the end of the ArrayList. 

Then a second test method is required and its name should start with the word "Test". 

The last block of code is a test method that calls the `PUT_ContainsContract` method, assuming that the `Contains` method always returns a `true`. This test ensures that `Contains` method correctly finds an item (`2`) within the list. It fails if `Contains` returns `false`, meaning there's no item `2` in the list.

#### Test Code Generation for Delete Operation

Now, let's focus on removing an item given a specific index.

```csharp
public class ArrayListContractTest
{
    public void PUT_RemoveContract([PexAssumeUnderTest]ArrayList arrList, int x)
    {
        AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(true);

        int Old_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
        int Old_arrListIndexOfX = arrList.IndexOf(x);

        arrList.RemoveAt(x);

        int New_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
        int New_arrListIndexOfX = arrList.IndexOf(x);

        PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$old_arrList_Count", Old_arrListCount);
        PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$new_arrList_Count", New_arrListCount);

        PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$old_arrList_IndexOf_x", Old_arrListIndexOfX);
        PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$new_arrList_IndexOf_x", New_arrListIndexOfX);

        try
        {
             // This line should execute without any exceptions
             Debug.Assert(
                    // If the return value is false, the item was successfully removed
                    -1 == New_arrListIndexOfX 
             );
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            // If there's an exception, write out an error message
            throw new Exception("The ArrayList.Remove method threw an exception. This is unexpected.", ex);
        }
    }

    [TestMethod]
    public void TestMethod2()
    {
        PexAssume.True(true);
        ArrayList arrList = new ArrayList();
        arrList.Add(1);
        arrList.Add(2);
        arrList.Add(3);

        PexParameterAttributesTest.PUT_RemoveContract(arrList, 1);
    }
}
```

Here, we're creating a test class that generates test code for the Remove method found in any ArrayList instance. This includes adding an item to the instance, trying to remove it, and finally verifying that it is no longer in the list. Note the test method's name prefix which should begin with the word "Test--------------------	    // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that  @@@ If the return value is fale, index of new array is = -1

            PexAssert.AreNotEqual<object>(Old_arrListCount, New_arrListCount);
            PexAssert.AreNotEqual<object>(Old_x, x);
            PexAssert.AreEqual<object>(Old_arrListIndexOfX, New_arrListIndexOfX);
            PexAssert.AreEqual<object>(Old_arrListLastIndexOfX, New_arrListLastIndexOfX);
            PexAssert.AreEqual<object>(Old_arrListIndexOfX >= 0, New_Ret);
            PexAssert.AreEqual<object>(New_arrListLastIndexOfX >= 0, New_Ret);
